EZ9rdb8OY2Bx7AaR8cIwhjc3fM4C5jmtJmwawTgYT0mAVSx84AXQn2H+osP0fSFK\nxZokgXWWNXs9gK/DPKAPx6LX9Zx/t69QFgZY1pnWB+e/YxsWlMMXEg6q8PCokclK\nDKdgFkskTD4YF6Gnw3XZd8zTw7SxlmVTMh9YholP9GMMkJk4GP/E5jQiV+bA1uVH\nWnvKpQLfgfr7IlYleandloqVovQet4ghIfrLD/ygjCdzjYNLp6jzrY5khbNDcDe+\n+ndtRxwvLSFrvaaHFE0TSSZlg14l2PXGFlyBVutUB5/Ds4SCjcb/VZaPtV3GEYym\n79lzAGfrRxuXk4lNrS41hsFRMp99Hin/6DecO0WCn4Q6OdkboWv4xys8NzLTJgY7\ntBlz+2xFpm+e7WBSlSXYJs3RyTb/Wd/jY3+MbtTmFYb/uxcIFt1aQvDApzSMAqCe\nE2kk7uUBF8pm/Cdn8rJ0\n=lkB6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b3221a25a40d75f7ad1a93579e5730ca080beabb\nparent d5ec93f379e742aad5902d0f70e7f0489ed7ad0b\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1779964561 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779964561 +0200\n\nStabilize Guardian client cache key handling (#24891)\n\nSplit from the Guardian prompt cache key change. This PR only updates\ncodex-rs/core/src/client.rs. Validation was not run per request; this\nbranch is expected to rely on the companion split PRs.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T10:36:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c95eb3d07bd7af4977d70bddfcaac925755da4c8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c95eb3d07bd7af4977d70bddfcaac925755da4c8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c95eb3d07bd7af4977d70bddfcaac925755da4c8/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d5ec93f379e742aad5902d0f70e7f0489ed7ad0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d5ec93f379e742aad5902d0f70e7f0489ed7ad0b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d5ec93f379e742aad5902d0f70e7f0489ed7ad0b"}]},{"sha":"d5ec93f379e742aad5902d0f70e7f0489ed7ad0b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ1ZWM5M2YzNzllNzQyYWFkNTkwMmQwZjcwZTdmMDQ4OWVkN2FkMGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T09:51:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T09:51:24Z"},"message":"Move memories root setup out of core config (#24758)\n\n## Why\n\nConfig loading should not create or write-authorize the memories root\njust because memory support exists. Memory startup is the code path that\nactually materializes that tree.\n\n## What\n\n- Stop creating the memories root during Config load and remove it from\nlegacy workspace-write projections.\n- Grant the memories root read access only when the memories feature and\nuse_memories are enabled.\n- Create the memories root inside memories startup before seeding\nextension instructions.\n- Update config and startup tests around the ownership boundary.\n\n## Tests\n\n- just fmt\n- just fix -p codex-core\n- just fix -p codex-memories-write\n- just test -p codex-core\nmemory_tool_makes_memories_root_readable_without_creating_or_widening_writes\nworkspace_write_includes_configured_writable_root_once_without_memories_root\npermission_profile_override_keeps_memories_root_out_of_legacy_projection\npermissions_profiles_allow_direct_write_roots_outside_workspace_root\ndefault_permissions_profile_populates_runtime_sandbox_policy\n- just test -p codex-memories-write memories_startup_creates_memory_root\n\nNote: a broader just test -p codex-core run is not clean in this\nsandbox; it hit missing test_stdio_server plus seatbelt, realtime, and\nenvironment-sensitive failures. The changed config tests above pass.","tree":{"sha":"149c5e22e38237e6806f211f5247f640df2f195b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/149c5e22e38237e6806f211f5247f640df2f195b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d5ec93f379e742aad5902d0f70e7f0489ed7ad0b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGBAcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY3gQAKpmI809i32a5h98hOBET+QY\nQB1UAqhE1NN6OXyYE9ON5y1kVhV62aATT7aR7Wf6MXym9HHZOyt+3pqgIByy7kSm\ngPYKan/fjwlLY0owON4wJupbQVvaIrwtD09ba8r/05/vxwMV+D2QTLzUuqk/u85w\n3f2AZ/ySqQUKTgmDHKOHY6Pua5TWvTHMxFgPQfVxtWussbZOV8jnnTgGU69kS3Sy\nl7DexE+L2Wf6RuYRIALA0DH3ISjCRil57rPUQ3xl+gpSTnL2AU4DT8mWnhn3GuOX\nq2PrwhCXRjQ4qhwhJ30Q4gxuZm1IRmBocwGP2vNGxmtf0F5XkfhGhgE707e/BO4W\nLVGjpH6g19gSvSZe0WxwasTymcMDPGAEi/QvNab4K+bUc4o53lUrrw4HmIHNY7hr\nlWlXWdhKIpFp7kvRD/CRvdEvM3ZPDArE/xYw756RlgOPCHIMN0V2wVb7Ppd299OJ\nCoy2CePFkmDsKs14aUjSSXsamROz0aPQFRdy3g6J/11JgVLnXf0955LIVFvAu/Ff\nF1j+TYXcwmLxb95BfSvi0XxVdGZkC/Jhf34qEappRBXmWYaCXzsHSK6Zl4CBgJIL\nC0vRxoisOZqtrP8Iz3oiJ9lKCQo3/HSohpt/dkJAESbzHsTKrbxl4sNsjhCPCgh+\nk5f7JJqbswgG8MVnAMKU\n=jWSA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 149c5e22e38237e6806f211f5247f640df2f195b\nparent 46946bb91c25b45dec125e29a933b019c61856ff\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1779961884 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779961884 +0200\n\nMove memories root setup out of core config (#24758)\n\n## Why\n\nConfig loading should not create or write-authorize the memories root\njust because memory support exists. Memory startup is the code path that\nactually materializes that tree.\n\n## What\n\n- Stop creating the memories root during Config load and remove it from\nlegacy workspace-write projections.\n- Grant the memories root read access only when the memories feature and\nuse_memories are enabled.\n- Create the memories root inside memories startup before seeding\nextension instructions.\n- Update config and startup tests around the ownership boundary.\n\n## Tests\n\n- just fmt\n- just fix -p codex-core\n- just fix -p codex-memories-write\n- just test -p codex-core\nmemory_tool_makes_memories_root_readable_without_creating_or_widening_writes\nworkspace_write_includes_configured_writable_root_once_without_memories_root\npermission_profile_override_keeps_memories_root_out_of_legacy_projection\npermissions_profiles_allow_direct_write_roots_outside_workspace_root\ndefault_permissions_profile_populates_runtime_sandbox_policy\n- just test -p codex-memories-write memories_startup_creates_memory_root\n\nNote: a broader just test -p codex-core run is not clean in this\nsandbox; it hit missing test_stdio_server plus seatbelt, realtime, and\nenvironment-sensitive failures. The changed config tests above pass.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T09:51:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d5ec93f379e742aad5902d0f70e7f0489ed7ad0b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d5ec93f379e742aad5902d0f70e7f0489ed7ad0b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d5ec93f379e742aad5902d0f70e7f0489ed7ad0b/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"46946bb91c25b45dec125e29a933b019c61856ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/46946bb91c25b45dec125e29a933b019c61856ff","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/46946bb91c25b45dec125e29a933b019c61856ff"}]},{"sha":"46946bb91c25b45dec125e29a933b019c61856ff","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ2OTQ2YmI5MWMyNWI0NWRlYzEyNWUyOWE5MzNiMDE5YzYxODU2ZmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T06:24:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T06:24:42Z"},"message":"[codex] Stage Python SDK beta versions from release tags (#24872)\n\n## Summary\n- Treat `sdk/python` as a development template with source version\n`0.0.0-dev`, matching the existing Python runtime packaging pattern.\n- Have `python-v*` tags supply the published SDK beta version through\nthe existing `stage-sdk --sdk-version` path.\n- Remove the workflow check requiring a source version bump for each\nbeta release and remove its now-unused host Python setup step.\n- Keep the reviewed runtime dependency pin at\n`openai-codex-cli-bin==0.132.0`.\n- Remove beta-number-specific documentation so it does not need editing\nfor each publish.\n\n## Why\nThe package staging script already writes the release version into the\nartifact. Requiring the checked-in SDK template version to match every\ntag adds release-only source churn without changing the package users\nreceive.\n\n## Validation\n- Not run locally; relying on online CI for this workflow and metadata\nchange.\n\n## Release\nAfter this PR lands, publish the next beta by pushing tag\n`python-v0.1.0b2` from merged `main`.","tree":{"sha":"6d283be6b5447584facc197ed11fa5cf457f3eb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6d283be6b5447584facc197ed11fa5cf457f3eb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/46946bb91c25b45dec125e29a933b019c61856ff","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqF9+qCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXt8QAA2q0R6WyjXTbiofrwC9IAXg\nOPhwqs96HrS/NFaGFHl0gwh/qV/N/2D1fYjwGO4We8VWeEStpipVRzCGFTmXBnXo\nrOaj+9vGYURf3jYjYE0Djf+9jSx9S+TzGUmVrkmhwPYImCpOTymJ+88Mug2D9WYo\n49GFLcTiD8XnvAzb0P2kor2GnaiTyWH5fQgxl2iZNtdth78eqv1grCJbFb77+cFE\naS3l+l8Ne5yL3aEEUL5Y+dG8sxl4jlGY+KKMVL5dszHqcBhOZsetd7U86lPZGX84\nZJkhConGeLuQ7yL8y4C08CHs8dPakdd2f3CwnUuuhWz9UqJiZABqQFtDcvF5GhJx\n7JcgBjftFCFmDzaihUIGXX3kqjYZFvMsLi31dP0sbi97tmaE99eJAeofFEL7m+Nd\n8j6pPaeYDpEw4oBPgnw5XI9xtnublgh8cvkZ+ZUUdstVaney5zKc3u2H0DPom7Gh\nfkRRvVivIk+JzxiiMkCwDacN0oApT/XtsMX2zllVrrURwTqSplzFYzj9ONmhHSNb\nXIzqa8WexUrHW8hmtsm+372btoBtPPY51flGk5/Whd4QtHH3yDu4cs6mI/XQQlg1\nasCzF8EjO0OQKbOyNlCBpA3U9SVdOlc/UkZXRswF5K0D1C7MKboNrxNlKQkpszBF\nLzB9ngHejrwkYT2Ojc0+\n=Z5Oc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6d283be6b5447584facc197ed11fa5cf457f3eb0\nparent 3d9f58ace8d77e1c1b083f4f2822154bb51eaae4\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1779949482 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779949482 -0700\n\n[codex] Stage Python SDK beta versions from release tags (#24872)\n\n## Summary\n- Treat `sdk/python` as a development template with source version\n`0.0.0-dev`, matching the existing Python runtime packaging pattern.\n- Have `python-v*` tags supply the published SDK beta version through\nthe existing `stage-sdk --sdk-version` path.\n- Remove the workflow check requiring a source version bump for each\nbeta release and remove its now-unused host Python setup step.\n- Keep the reviewed runtime dependency pin at\n`openai-codex-cli-bin==0.132.0`.\n- Remove beta-number-specific documentation so it does not need editing\nfor each publish.\n\n## Why\nThe package staging script already writes the release version into the\nartifact. Requiring the checked-in SDK template version to match every\ntag adds release-only source churn without changing the package users\nreceive.\n\n## Validation\n- Not run locally; relying on online CI for this workflow and metadata\nchange.\n\n## Release\nAfter this PR lands, publish the next beta by pushing tag\n`python-v0.1.0b2` from merged `main`.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T06:24:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/46946bb91c25b45dec125e29a933b019c61856ff","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/46946bb91c25b45dec125e29a933b019c61856ff","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/46946bb91c25b45dec125e29a933b019c61856ff/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.git